# Test: ze doctor reports a plugin declared in-process only configured external.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-doctor-coverage-12-plugin-infra AC-24 -- `ze doctor` reads
#            Registration.RunsInProcessOnly of the plugin an external block
#            runs and reports doctor-plugin-external-unsupported, with the fix
#            "move it to an internal block". The registration is the test-only
#            internal/test/plugins/fakeinprocess (linked by the zetest build).
# PREVENTS:  an external block starting a forked process that silently does
#            nothing, with doctor reporting a clean box.
#
# Revert checkExternalInProcess (internal/component/plugin/doctor/check_external.go)
# or the field on the fixture and the code leaves stdout.
#
# The block is named in-process-probe, not after the plugin, so the registry
# holds only the name the `run` line resolves to (ResolvePlugin: `ze plugin X`
# answers X). A check that looked the registration up by the block name would
# find none and print no row. The row names both, the block in its message and
# its fix, the registration after "runs" (externalInProcessRow), and the
# expectations read both.

tmpfs=in-process.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
	external in-process-probe {
		run "ze plugin fake-in-process-only"
	}
}

bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote { ip 127.0.0.1; }
			local { ip 127.0.0.1; accept false; }
		}
		session {
			asn { local 65000; remote 65001; }
			router-id 1.2.3.4;
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json config in-process.conf
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-plugin-external-unsupported
expect=stdout:contains=runs fake-in-process-only, which works only inside the daemon
expect=stdout:contains=move it to an internal block: plugin { internal in-process-probe { use fake-in-process-only; } }
